<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  OpenFreshr entitlements — deliberately empty.

  OpenFreshr ships as a direct-distribution Developer ID app under the hardened
  runtime (ENABLE_HARDENED_RUNTIME=YES) and is NOT sandboxed
  (ENABLE_APP_SANDBOX=NO), because it must write to /Applications to replace apps
  in place. App Store distribution is an explicit non-goal.

  A non-sandboxed hardened-runtime app needs NO entitlement for anything
  OpenFreshr actually does. Every capability below was checked against the code
  and is intentionally NOT requested:

    * Spawning subprocesses (brew, mas, msupdate, codesign, spctl via
      Sources/OpenFreshrCore/Platform/ProcessRunning.swift) — the hardened runtime
      does not gate spawning separate, independently-signed processes.
    * Outbound network (URLSession in Platform/HTTPFetching.swift) —
      com.apple.security.network.client is a SANDBOX entitlement and has no effect
      here; unsandboxed network access needs no entitlement.
    * Launch-at-login (SMAppService.mainApp in SettingsView.swift) — the modern
      login-item API needs no entitlement for a non-sandboxed app.
    * User notifications (UNUserNotificationCenter) — need no entitlement.
    * Apple events — the app sends none (no NSAppleScript/osascript/AEDetermine),
      so com.apple.security.automation.apple-events is NOT requested.
    * Loading third-party code — the app loads no external dylibs or plug-ins, so
      com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation is NOT requested. Sparkle,
      when linked for a release, ships its framework and XPC services signed by
      the SAME Developer ID team, so library validation still passes without this
      exception (Sparkle only needs it for SANDBOXED hosts).
    * No JIT / no unsigned executable memory / no DYLD env vars — none of the
      cs.allow-* hardened-runtime exceptions are needed.

  If a future capability genuinely requires an entitlement, add it here WITH a
  justification comment and mirror it into docs/release/entitlements/openfreshr.plist
  so the notarization broker signs with the identical set.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
